# Sample requests for every scenario. Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension and click "Send Request".
# Start everything first with ./run.sh. Sections match the root cause analyses in docs/.
@policy = http://localhost:5001
@billing = http://localhost:5002
@recon = http://localhost:5003

### Bind a new policy
POST {{policy}}/api/policies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "insuredName": "Acme Dental Group",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
  "annualPremium": 1200,
  "feeAmount": 50,
  "commissionRate": 0.15
}

### Endorse it midterm (annual +600, prorated by the service)
POST {{policy}}/api/policies/PS-000001/endorsements
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveDate": "2026-07-02",
  "annualPremiumChange": 600
}

### Cancel it
POST {{policy}}/api/policies/PS-000001/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveDate": "2026-10-01"
}

### Policy view
GET {{policy}}/api/policies/PS-000001

### Billing view of the same policy
GET {{billing}}/api/billing/accounts/PS-000001

### Generate 100 test policies
POST {{policy}}/api/dev/seed?count=100

### Send a bad transaction straight to billing (should be rejected with 400)
POST {{billing}}/api/inbound/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "policyNumber": "PS-999999",
  "sequence": 2,
  "type": "Cancellation",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-05-01",
  "premiumChange": 250.005,
  "feeAmount": 0,
  "commissionRate": 0.9
}

### ========== Duplicate submission (RCA 001) ==========
### Send this SAME request twice: 201 the first time, 200 the second (nothing new booked).
POST {{billing}}/api/inbound/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "policyNumber": "PS-DUP-001",
  "sequence": 1,
  "type": "NewBusiness",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
  "premiumChange": 1200,
  "feeAmount": 50,
  "commissionRate": 0.15
}

### Billing account for the duplicate test (count the rows, check the commission)
GET {{billing}}/api/billing/accounts/PS-DUP-001

### Same TransactionId, different premium: rejected with 409
POST {{billing}}/api/inbound/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "policyNumber": "PS-DUP-001",
  "sequence": 1,
  "type": "NewBusiness",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
  "premiumChange": 1300,
  "feeAmount": 50,
  "commissionRate": 0.15
}

### ========== Retries and the error queue (RCA 002) ==========
### Sync status: how many transactions are Sent, Failed (retrying), or DeadLettered
GET {{policy}}/api/sync/status

### Transactions waiting for an automatic retry
GET {{policy}}/api/sync/retrying

### Error queue: gave up, needs a person
GET {{policy}}/api/sync/errors

### Resend one from the error queue (paste a transactionId from the list above)
POST {{policy}}/api/sync/errors/99b3f822-2aa5-42f2-91b8-4d02c5338191/resend

### ========== Out-of-order transactions (RCA 003) ==========
### Set this to the policy number returned by the bind below
@orderPolicy = PS-000001

### 1. Bind (billing UP)
POST {{policy}}/api/policies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "insuredName": "Order Test LLC",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
  "annualPremium": 1200,
  "feeAmount": 0,
  "commissionRate": 0.15
}

### 2. Endorse (stop billing BEFORE sending this one)
POST {{policy}}/api/policies/{{orderPolicy}}/endorsements
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveDate": "2026-07-02",
  "annualPremiumChange": 600
}

### 3. Cancel (start billing again, then send this RIGHT AWAY)
POST {{policy}}/api/policies/{{orderPolicy}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveDate": "2026-10-01"
}

### What billing has for this policy (check right after step 3, then again a minute later)
GET {{billing}}/api/billing/accounts/{{orderPolicy}}

### Billing's booking order: newest first, the id shows the order rows were booked
GET {{billing}}/api/billing/transactions?take=10

### Transactions held behind an earlier one
GET {{policy}}/api/sync/held

### Billing guard: sequence 3 for a policy billing has never seen (rejected with 425)
POST {{billing}}/api/inbound/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "policyNumber": "PS-ORDER-999",
  "sequence": 3,
  "type": "Cancellation",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-05-01",
  "premiumChange": -100,
  "feeAmount": 0,
  "commissionRate": 0.15
}

### ========== Cancellation math and commission drift (RCA 004) ==========
### Cancellation math: use the out-of-order section's Bind / Endorse / Cancel (billing up the whole time),
### then compare the policy's writtenPremium to the hand calculation:
###   earned = 1,200 x 273/365 + 600 x 91/365 = 1,047.12
GET {{policy}}/api/policies/{{orderPolicy}}

### Commission drift: $1,000 at 12.5% plus 20 endorsements of +$1.00. Compares policy vs. billing commission.
POST {{policy}}/api/dev/drift-demo?endorsements=20

### ========== Negative premium and $0 boundaries (RCA 005) ==========
### Bind a fresh policy for these (set @edgePolicy to the number it returns)
@edgePolicy = PS-000001

POST {{policy}}/api/policies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "insuredName": "Edge Case LLC",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
  "annualPremium": 1200,
  "feeAmount": 0,
  "commissionRate": 0.15
}

### A. Reduce premium below $0 (annual -2,000 on a 1,200 policy)
POST {{policy}}/api/policies/{{edgePolicy}}/endorsements
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
  "annualPremiumChange": -2000
}

### B. Cancel the policy (send AFTER A to see the knock-on effect)
POST {{policy}}/api/policies/{{edgePolicy}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveDate": "2026-06-01"
}

### C. Cancel on the expiration date (use a different fresh policy number)
POST {{policy}}/api/policies/PS-000002/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveDate": "2027-01-01"
}

### What billing has for the edge-case policy
GET {{billing}}/api/billing/accounts/{{edgePolicy}}

### Billing guard: a direct endorsement that would take the account below $0 (rejected with 400)
POST {{billing}}/api/inbound/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333",
  "policyNumber": "{{edgePolicy}}",
  "sequence": 2,
  "type": "Endorsement",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
  "premiumChange": -2000,
  "feeAmount": 0,
  "commissionRate": 0.15
}

### ========== Reconciliation ==========

### Run a reconciliation now (policy and billing must have been started at least once)
POST {{recon}}/api/recon/runs

### Most recent run: counts by reason code
GET {{recon}}/api/recon/runs/latest

### Run history
GET {{recon}}/api/recon/runs

### Findings for a run (change the run id)
GET {{recon}}/api/recon/runs/3/findings

### Only one reason code: MissingInBilling, StuckInQueue, MissingInPolicy, PremiumMismatch, FeeMismatch, CommissionMismatch, StatusMismatch
GET {{recon}}/api/recon/runs/1/findings?reason=StuckInQueue

### Only one policy
GET {{recon}}/api/recon/runs/1/findings?policy=PS-000001

### ========== Inject discrepancies (Development only, RCA 006) ==========
### Seed first so there are healthy policies to corrupt
POST {{policy}}/api/dev/seed?count=100

### Run a clean reconciliation first: should be 0 findings
POST {{recon}}/api/recon/runs

### Kinds you can inject
GET {{recon}}/api/dev/inject/kinds

### Inject one of every kind, each on a different policy (the response says what each should produce)
POST {{recon}}/api/dev/inject/all

### Or inject a single kind (optionally add &policy=PS-000123)
POST {{recon}}/api/dev/inject?kind=EarnedPremiumMismatch

### Reconcile again: every reason code should show up
POST {{recon}}/api/recon/runs

### The "both systems agree and both are wrong" finding (change the run id)
GET {{recon}}/api/recon/runs/2/findings?reason=EarnedPremiumMismatch
